{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). Reporter: Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, non-VIP), from her own verified email. Says she likely left work laptop in an Uber last night; unsure if it was locked. Device: BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15), assigned to her. Device status shows ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:57 UTC (Sat ~21:57 Chicago), no warnings, 14.6% disk free. Sign-in logs (14 days): 10 sign-ins, all Chicago, Duo push, usual hours, no failures, no hosting networks; nothing after Oct 9 so no suspicious activity seen yet. Data at risk: Ops/logistics work data, M365 mailbox (99.4% full) and cached sessions, VPN access. Actions: block_sign_in queued pending technician approval. Needed from Tier 2: remote lock (and wipe if not recovered) of BL-LT-0109 while it is online, revoke sessions/tokens, plan password reset by phone after verification, unblock once secured. Asked user for when/where last seen, lock state, and to file Uber lost-item report / police report if stolen.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation for all lost devices to remote lock/wipe; ticket is P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for telling us so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. Your laptop checked in to our system late last night and still shows as online, so I've passed it to our Tier 2 team. They can lock it remotely and, if it isn't found, erase it. I've also asked a technician to temporarily block sign-ins and VPN access on your account so nobody can use a saved session on the laptop. That block isn't in place yet. It starts once a technician approves it, and after that you won't be able to sign in until we reset your password. We'll do that over the phone once we've confirmed it's you. To help us, please reply with: (1) roughly what time and where you last had the laptop, (2) whether you think it was locked or asleep, and (3) the trip details from your Uber app. Please also report the lost item through the Uber app, and if you think it was stolen, file a police report. If you get the laptop back, let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 P1. Ticket came from the user's own verified email. User 9 Mei Chen, account active, not VIP. Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:57 UTC (~21:57 Chicago). Sign-in logs: 10 sign-ins over 14 days, all Chicago, Duo push, within usual hours, none after Oct 9. No suspicious activity so far. Lock state unknown and the device is online while possibly in someone else's hands, so I queued block_sign_in (approval id 1). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for remote lock/wipe, session/token revocation, a password reset by phone after identity check, then unblock. Asked the user for last-seen time/place, lock state and trip details, and to report it to Uber (and police if stolen). Side note: mailbox is 99.4% full.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021",
    "KB-018"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
